\chapter{Control Plane Structure}

There should be something more detailed to say here, but this is as much
as has been written thus far.

\section{Framekernels: Continuations and State Machines}

Rust appears to have a way to support continuation-passing style.
Within a framekernel domain, state machines and continuations are the
fundamental control flow dispatch mechanism.

\section{Multikernels: Network Protocol Like Message Passing}

Between the multikernel's partitions or subdomains, microkernel-style
message passing is handled in an explicitly network protocol handling
-oriented fashion.
